        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "7"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Digit sum",
        "body": "BENJAMIN has 7 different letters B, E, N, J, A, M, I, so they use all of the digits 1 to 7 (sum 28), and N appears twice. The digit sum is $28 + N$.\n\nDivisible by 3: $28 + N$ is a multiple of 3, so $N = 2$ or $N = 5$. The number is odd and ends in N, so $N = 5$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 5**"
