    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The sum of five different positive integers is 17. How many different values can their product take?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "List all possibilities",
        "body": "The smallest possible sum of five different positive integers is $1+2+3+4+5 = 15$. We need 2 more, and the numbers must stay different. The only ways:\n- add 2 to the largest: $1, 2, 3, 4, 7$ (product 168);\n- add 1 to each of the two largest: $1, 2, 3, 5, 6$ (product 180).\n\n(Adding to a smaller number would make two numbers equal unless the larger ones are raised as well, which costs more than 2.) So there are 2 possible products.\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory",
      "counting"
    ],
