    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Tonight I am meeting five of my friends: Andrew; Boris; Chris; Dan; and Eugene. Andrew has already met one of them, Boris – two of them, Chris – three of them, and Dan – four of them. How many of them has Eugene already met?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "0"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Start with Dan and Andrew",
        "body": "Dan has met 4 of the others — all of them. So Andrew's only acquaintance is Dan.\n\nChris has met 3 of the others, but not Andrew: so Chris has met Boris, Dan and Eugene.\n\nBoris has met 2: Dan and Chris (both know him), so not Eugene.\n\nEugene has met Dan and Chris: 2 of them.\n\n**Answer: (C) 2**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count meetings",
        "body": "Each meeting between two friends is counted twice in the total $1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + e$, so this total is even and $e$ is even: $e = 0, 2$ or $4$. Dan knows everyone, so $e \\ge 1$; Andrew knows only Dan, so $e \\le 3$. Hence $e = 2$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 2**"
      }
    ],
