    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Compare the directions of the arms",
        "body": "The solid is a column of cubes with an arm at the top and an arm at the bottom. The two arms point in **perpendicular** directions (the top arm runs to the right, the bottom cube sticks out towards the front). Rotating the solid cannot change this, and it also keeps the order of light and dark cubes along the chain.\n\nIn (B) the two end arms point the same way, so the solid would be flat like a C or U — that is a different solid. The other pictures show the solid from different sides.\n\n**Answer: (B)**"
