        "text": "66 cm"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "54 cm"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "60 cm"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Track the perimeter",
        "body": "Let the cut-off corner triangles have sides $x$, $y$, $z$. Cutting off a corner triangle of side $x$ removes $2x$ from the perimeter (two pieces of the big triangle's sides) and adds $x$ (the new cut edge): the perimeter goes down by $x$.\n\nSo $60 - (x + y + z) = 40$ and $x + y + z = 20$. The three triangles have perimeters $3x + 3y + 3z = 60$ cm.\n\n**Answer: (E) 60 cm**"
      }
    ],
