        "text": "52"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "58"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "68"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "72"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count small triangles",
        "body": "Cut the triangle into 5 rows of equal height. Each row can be split into small equilateral triangles of the same size as the top one: the rows contain $1, 3, 5, 7, 9$ small triangles (25 in total).\n\nIn the diagram the 1st, 3rd and 5th regions (from the top) are shaded: $1 + 5 + 9 = 15$ of 25 small triangles, i.e. $\\frac{15}{25} = 60\\%$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 60**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Similar triangles",
        "body": "The triangles cut off from the top by the lines have sides $\\frac15, \\frac25, \\dots$ of the big one, so areas $\\frac{1}{25}, \\frac{4}{25}, \\frac{9}{25}, \\frac{16}{25}, 1$. The shaded regions: $\\frac{1}{25} + (\\frac{9}{25} - \\frac{4}{25}) + (1 - \\frac{16}{25}) = \\frac{15}{25} = 60\\%$.\n\n**Answer: (A)**"
      }
    ],
